    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1031-a3">

                <pb facs="1138" n="1042" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1042"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 194.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-27T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                                1898—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>(Received March 28, 8.30
                        a.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodford</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister, Madrid:</hi></p>
                <p>With reference to the first part of the Saturday memorandum, you may explain that
                    the captain of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi> merely sought permission
                    to employ small explosive charges on upper works to clear away wreckage and get
                    at bodies and guns, but finding his request misunderstood and opposed he
                    withdrew it under instructions from the Secretary of the Navy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
